From: Codex M2 final image verification
Subject: [PATCH] Check integrated runtime and ADB artifacts inside actual ext4 images

Reason: new runtime source/staging checks do not establish that final filesystem
packing retains the same files, modes and labels. Extend the existing image
verification stage after sparse conversion; no image/device writes.
Files: existing verify_exynos9810_images.sh and one read-only debugfs helper.
Verify: actual system/vendor ext4 bytes against verified staging, selected modes,
donor-matched ownership (cameraserver0:2000) and SELinux labels; include compiled SettingsProvider/services
artifacts already checked by mandatory ADB gate. Default profiles unchanged.
Rollback: reverse source patch; generated images/retained ROMs are not removed.
Actual build/runtime results: parent docs/m2-integrated-runtime-build.md.

diff --git a/scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_images.sh b/scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_images.sh
--- a/scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_images.sh
+++ b/scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_images.sh
@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@
                 fi
                 echo "Verified distinct libPSI.so/libpsi.so in actual $PARTITION image"
             fi
+            if [ "${EXYNOS9810_M2_RUNTIME_COMPAT:-false}" = "true" ] && \
